<head>
  <title>Template syntax — Azox</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Interpolation, event handlers, dynamic attributes and literal text in .azox files." />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css" />
  <script src="/site.js" defer></script>
</head>

<script>
  import Nav from '../../components/Nav.azox';
  import Footer from '../../components/Footer.azox';
  import DocsNav from '../../components/DocsNav.azox';
  import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.azox';
</script>

<div class="shell">
  <Nav version="0.2.0" current="docs" />

  <div class="container docs">
    <DocsNav current="/docs/syntax" />

    <main class="doc-body">
      <h1>Template syntax</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A <code>.azox</code> file is HTML with three additions: braces for
        expressions, <code>on:</code> for events, and optional
        <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> blocks.
        It is not JSX — attributes keep their HTML names, and there is no
        <code>className</code>.
      </p>

      <h2>File structure</h2>

      <CodeBlock label="anatomy"><text><head>
  <!-- optional: copied into the document head -->
  <title>My page</title>
</head>

<script>
  // optional: imports and state
  import { signal } from 'azox/reactivity';
  const count = signal(0);
</script>

<main>
  <!-- the markup, exactly one root element -->
</main></text></CodeBlock>

      <div class="note">
        <p>
          A page needs a single root element in its markup, the way a document
          has one <code>&lt;body&gt;</code>. Wrap siblings in a container.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Interpolation</h2>
      <p>Braces evaluate an expression and insert the result as text.</p>

      <CodeBlock label="interpolation"><text><p>Hello, {name()}</p>
<p>Total: {price() * quantity()}</p>
<p>{items().length} items</p></text></CodeBlock>

      <p>
        Values are escaped, so text that looks like markup is shown, not
        interpreted.
      </p>

      <h2>Attributes</h2>
      <p>Quoted values are static; braces make an attribute reactive.</p>

      <CodeBlock label="attributes"><text><div class="card">static</div>

<div class={theme()}>reactive</div>
<img src={user().avatar} alt="Avatar" />
<a href={'/user/' + id()}>Profile</a></text></CodeBlock>

      <p>
        A reactive attribute gets its own effect, so it updates independently
        of everything else on the page.
      </p>

      <h2>Events</h2>
      <p>
        Prefix any DOM event with <code>on:</code>. The expression is used as
        the listener directly.
      </p>

      <CodeBlock label="events"><text><button on:click={() => count.set(count() + 1)}>
  Add one
</button>

<input on:input={(e) => name.set(e.target.value)} />

<form on:submit={handleSubmit}>
  <button type="submit">Send</button>
</form></text></CodeBlock>

      <div class="note">
        <p>
          Handlers can contain object literals and nested braces —
          <code>on:click={'{'}() =&gt; user.set({'{'} name: 'Ada' {'}'}){'}'}</code>
          parses correctly.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Literal text</h2>
      <p>
        To show markup or braces as-is — a code sample, for instance — wrap it
        in <code>&lt;text&gt;</code>. Nothing inside is parsed as markup or
        interpolated.
      </p>

      <CodeBlock label="literal text"><text><pre><text><button on:click={handler}>Not parsed</button></text></pre></text></CodeBlock>

      <p>This documentation is written in Azox and uses it for every snippet.</p>

      <h2>Comments</h2>

      <CodeBlock label="comments"><text><!-- an HTML comment, kept in the output -->

<script>
  // a JavaScript comment, stripped from the output
</script></text></CodeBlock>

      <h2>Reference</h2>

      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Syntax</th>
              <th>Meaning</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><code>{'{'}expr{'}'}</code></td>
              <td>Insert the value of an expression, escaped</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>attr={'{'}expr{'}'}</code></td>
              <td>A reactive attribute</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>attr="value"</code></td>
              <td>A static attribute</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>on:event={'{'}fn{'}'}</code></td>
              <td>Attach a DOM event listener</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>&lt;Capitalised /&gt;</code></td>
              <td>A component</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>&lt;slot /&gt;</code></td>
              <td>Where a component places its children</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>&lt;text&gt;…&lt;/text&gt;</code></td>
              <td>Literal content, never parsed</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>Next</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/docs/components">Components</a> — splitting a page up</li>
        <li><a href="/docs/routing">Routing</a> — turning files into URLs</li>
      </ul>
    </main>
  </div>

  <Footer />
</div>
